'''''Austrocylindropuntia cylindrica''''' (syn. ''Opuntia cylindrica''), the '''cane cactus''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Cactaceae]]. 

== Distribution and habitat ==
It is native to Colombia, Ecuador, and Peru, and it has been introduced to the [[Canary Islands]], Morocco, Eritrea, Ethiopia, South Africa, Australia, and New Zealand.<ref name="128942-1">{{cite POWO |id=128942-1 |title=''Austrocylindropuntia cylindrica'' (Lam.) Backeb. |access-date=29 May 2022 }}</ref> A popular ornamental, it is an invasive species in Europe, South Africa, and Australia.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.cabi.org/isc/datasheet/112618 |title=Datasheet ''Austrocylindropuntia cylindrica'' (cane cactus) |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2022 |website=Invasive Species Compendium |publisher=CAB International |access-date=29 May 2022 |quote=...Common Names ...coral cactus }}</ref> Due to a misidentification, for a time this species was erroneously thought to contain [[mescaline]].<ref>{{cite book |title=Stimulants |last1=Iversen |first1=Leslie |date=6 December 2012 |page=260-261 |isbn=9781475705102 }}</ref>
